WEBVTT

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:02.980
Inter-high

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:02.980
Day 3

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.740
This bath is so big and wonderful!

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:09.730
It is.

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:11.930
Really.

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:16.300
Good morning.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.730
You're awake!

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:20.330
Did you see anything?

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:24.640
Yes. I remembered something about 
last year's inter-high tournament.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.250
The matches?

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:30.550
No, something that happened 
after the tournament.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:35.090
Kagoshima - Kirishima

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:35.090
One year ago

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:35.090
Great work at the 
inter-highschool tournament.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.190
I saw the finals on TV.

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:39.900
Shame how it turned out.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.370
There were so many strong players.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.350
We couldn't win.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:49.860
I had a lot of fun though, 
playing mahjong with everyone.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:54.950
Next year, I'll be going, too!

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:56.820
What? Really?

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:57.660
Yeah!

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:03.040
I'll help so that you won't have to bear 
all of the burden again, like this year!

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:06.530
Is what you say, but aren't you just jealous?

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:08.580
That's obviously part of it, too.

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:12.290
But if that means we'll have 
another mahjong player,

00:01:12.290 --> 00:01:13.590
that makes me very happy!

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:16.590
Next year, Haruru will be in high school, too.

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:20.060
Which means that next year, 
we from the branch family

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:21.780
get to form a team with the princess!

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.810
We're gonna go straight to 
the top at Nationals!

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:31.610
That was a year ago.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:35.070
We've made it to the 
inter-high tournament again.

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:37.560
Today's day three.

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.600
So we'll go up against 
the teams that win today.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.100
<b>28 Makabi High (Okinawa) 
29 Miyamori Girls' (Iwate) 
30 Ihonosho High (Yamaguchi) 
31 Tateyama Business School (Chiba)</b>

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:44.300
I wonder who's going to win.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:43.600
<b>35 Kogasaki Business School (Fukui) 
 36 Karouto High (Hiroshima) 
37 Hida Business School (Gifu) 
38 Himematsu High (South Osaka) 
39 Kuratsuki High (Ishikawa)</b>

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.290
<b>32 Nogomi High (Saga) 
33 Kiyosumi High (Nagano) 
34 Chiyomi High (Tottori) 
35 Kogasaki Business School (Fukui)</b>

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:49.590
I had the same feeling at our training camp,

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:52.520
but there's something sad 
about hanging school uniforms

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.050
in ryokan and hotel closets.

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:56.300
What are you mumbling about?

00:01:56.990 --> 00:01:57.930
Okay, then!

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:01.930
Time for our first Nationals match!

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:05.030
Get up, get up!

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:30.400
That reminds me.

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:32.690
Are you okay with not seeing your sister,

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.840
even though we came all the way to Tokyo?

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:36.900
Yes.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:39.970
She didn't really talk to me 
the last time we met, either.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:43.260
But if it's mahjong...

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:47.520
If I meet her through mahjong, 
I feel like I could talk to her.

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:51.160
I suppose...

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.070
I looked at the pairings, and my sister's school

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:58.900
is in the other block.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.190
So I can't go up against her

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:04.970
unless we make it to the finals.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:10.790
That's why... they're all going down.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.980
<b>The Nationals</b>

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:47.700
<b>Hand 2: 
Support</b>

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:45.770
Wow, it's so big,

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:47.950
I feel like I'll get lost again.

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:51.310
If you do, just make it back 
before the fifth players' match.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:53.870
We ask our guests with small children

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:57.060
to please hold their child's hand at all times.

00:04:58.410 --> 00:04:59.380
Saki!

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:01.320
Nonoka!

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:02.650
Good luck!

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:04.140
Destroy them!

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:05.230
Koromo-cha—

00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:06.360
Koromo-san?

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:08.250
Haramura Nodoka.

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:10.580
If you lose, I'm making you my maid.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:12.500
That's an ingenious scheme!

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:13.450
Um, no...

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:15.610
Noppo's school!

00:05:15.610 --> 00:05:18.330
How did they arrive at "maid"?

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.300
All right.

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:21.160
We're going to the auditorium.

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:22.950
We await news of your victory!

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:24.990
Hisa.

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:29.720
Hey.

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:31.890
So, it's finally time.

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:34.060
Thanks for coming!

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:37.590
We're not the only ones cheering for you.

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:41.030
There's an event to screen Kiyosumi's matches

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:42.360
and cheer you all on,

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:45.440
at the hall where the preliminaries took place.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:49.440
People have gathered to watch on the 
street screens and cheer you on, too

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:53.470
Wahaha. It's that "public viewing" thing.

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:57.220
Come on, don't make me nervous!

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:00.210
Oh, just a second.

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:04.950
Hmm, our student congress vice president 
said he'd only call if it was urgent...

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:06.870
Hey, what's up?

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:09.080
I'm going to be mad if this isn't urgent!

00:06:09.730 --> 00:06:12.930
Um, well, actually...

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.580
Gimme that!

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:15.820
Good luck, Pres!

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:17.140
We're rooting for you!

00:06:17.590 --> 00:06:19.140
Thanks.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:22.780
Anyway, I sent you a URL by email.

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:23.900
Bye!

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:27.230
He's always so weird.

00:06:27.230 --> 00:06:30.110
Did he send me student congress 
work even at a time like this?

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:30.570
All right.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:33.150
We're heading to the auditorium.

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:36.080
Sorry that we couldn't really talk...

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:38.170
Good luck!

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:39.470
Good lucks!

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:41.100
Thank you!

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:46.840
<i>Well then...</i>

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:53.720
Wow, the green room is so huge!

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:56.390
They really have 12 of these?

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:58.730
It's bigger than our café.

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:01.220
This is nice.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:02.230
All right!

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:03.940
Let's get right to it!

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:07.150
Kyoutarou, where are <i>they</i>?

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:13.820
These are my special tacos!

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.950
They're delicious!

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:20.970
You've gotten better!

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:23.420
I got some tips from someone 
who knows tacos well.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:25.330
You mean a Mexican?!

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:26.840
No, remember at the 
prefectural preliminaries,

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:30.780
when you asked me to find 
tacos in the morning?

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:35.790
There was this guy who told 
me about a place close by.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.570
I ran into him again this time 
in the lodge, somehow,

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:41.520
and he showed me how to make good tacos.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.700
Looks like you found a good teacher!

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:47.900
He can do anything, really.

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:52.070
Oh, it's a video.

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:54.290
The thing from your vice president?

00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:55.280
Yeah...

00:07:55.770 --> 00:07:58.540
"Watch this together"?

00:08:00.050 --> 00:08:02.440
I wonder if this will work.

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:04.240
Maybe it's some porn video!

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:05.420
Of course it isn't.

00:08:06.770 --> 00:08:07.940
Oh, it worked.

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:09.550
It's the vice president!

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:12.490
<i>Pres, you said that cheerleading 
teams and send-off parties</i>

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:14.260
<i>were not your thing.</i>

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:15.430
<i>But since you won the 
prefectural preliminaries,</i>

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:17.020
<i>the number of Kiyosumi 
Mahjong Club fans</i>

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:19.900
<i>among our students, parents, and 
teachers has been increasing...</i>

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:20.310
Huh?

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:25.350
<i>So today, we're using the school 
gym to hold a support event!</i>

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:29.170
<i>Take a look inside...</i>

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:34.280
<i>And now, I'd like to present 
you their messages of support.</i>

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:36.210
There's so many people!

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:38.030
<i>Good luck, Kataoka-san.</i>

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:41.200
It's our homeroom teacher Sasahina!

00:08:41.550 --> 00:08:44.460
<i>You'll get one rice ball for each win.</i>

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:46.670
And that's the lunch lady.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:49.550
<i>Good luck, everyone!</i>

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:51.590
Muro's in the background!

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:54.510
Looks like the lolicon suspicions 
about our co-captain were founded.

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:57.800
<i>I'll make you taco-ramen once you're back.</i>

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:00.150
The ramen guy!

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:04.100
<i>Back when I was a first year...</i>

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:07.810
<i>I was the only one in the club the entire year.</i>

00:09:08.370 --> 00:09:12.820
<i>Mako came my second year, and 
for that year, it was the two of us.</i>

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:17.340
<i>And now, we have all these people.</i>

00:09:23.010 --> 00:09:26.460
<i>And that's it for our support messages.</i>

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:28.830
<i>I'll call and send the email now.</i>

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:31.960
<i>I figure you won't see it unless I call.</i>

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:34.920
<i>This counts as an urgent message, right?</i>

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:37.880
This makes me happy.

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:41.080
Yes.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:44.080
It's not like we have a 
cheerleading group traveling with us

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:45.940
all the way to Tokyo, 
like they did for Kazekoshi.

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:46.890
Hang on.

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:50.410
You don't have to bring up Kazekoshi 
to hide your embarrassment.

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:52.110
Can't you just enjoy it?

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:54.060
You're right.

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:55.890
<i>I'm grateful.</i>

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:01.280
We've got to give it our best.

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:02.660
Yeah!

00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:03.920
<i>That's right.</i>

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:07.410
<i>We have done everything we can to prepare.</i>

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:17.440
I'd like to thank you all for 
agreeing to this mixed training camp.

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:14.250
<b>Welcome</b>

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:14.800
<b>Participants in the 
Kiyosumi High Mahjong Club
Four Schools' 
Mixed Training Camp</b>

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:19.800
I'm sure you're all tired from the trip,

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:22.610
so we'd like to make the 
rest of this day a free day.

00:10:22.610 --> 00:10:24.220
Sounds good!

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:27.870
Saki!

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:29.430
Nonoka!

00:10:29.430 --> 00:10:30.850
Koromo-san!

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:32.840
Let's play together!

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:34.600
Okay. What should we play?

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:35.690
Mahjong!

00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:38.490
Let's play nonstop, day and night!

00:10:38.910 --> 00:10:40.260
This is nice.

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:41.530
Sure is.

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:46.590
Ahh, this is divine.

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:51.090
Hey, you're from Kazekoshi.

00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:52.360
I'm Yoshitome.

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:54.000
Yoshitome Miharu.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:56.510
Nice job in the second players' match.

00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:59.390
But I didn't do anything.

00:10:59.390 --> 00:11:02.050
It was more the yakuman that Tsuruga girl got.

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:04.540
Yeah, that was a bummer.

00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:06.520
I'd like some payback at some point.

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:08.110
Agreed.

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:09.370
Who are you?!

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:19.440
Ah, you're from Ryuumonbuchi.

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:20.530
Yeah.

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:23.030
This is perfect! Let's have a rematch!

00:11:23.030 --> 00:11:24.670
Yoshitome-san...

00:11:24.670 --> 00:11:25.470
Yes?

00:11:26.860 --> 00:11:29.670
You're totally flat.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:32.980
Harsh! You didn't have to compare!

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:34.920
Sorry. I couldn't help it.

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:37.500
So here's the bath, wahaha.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:39.780
<i>Another person with a flat chest!</i>

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:43.260
It's bigger than I thought.

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:44.970
Speaking of...

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:46.600
We're all here.

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:48.900
You're my enemy in another area, too!

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:49.860
Huh?

00:11:53.510 --> 00:11:56.230
She got another yakuman...

00:11:56.710 --> 00:12:00.170
And my favorite yakuman, at that.

00:12:00.170 --> 00:12:02.900
My deepest condolences.

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:05.180
What's wrong, Miharun?

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:07.120
Leave me alone, Kana-chan.

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:08.870
<b>Ryuumonbuchi High School 
Team Members</b>

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:10.380
Tomoki...

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:12.440
This is like a horror movie.

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:18.170
Touka?

00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:35.480
I got lost!

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:39.980
Was Kazekoshi's room even on this floor?

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:43.690
We'll catch a chill if we don't get back soon.

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:47.860
Oh, I found Tsuruga's room!

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:49.620
But that's got nothing to do with it.

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:51.240
I'm coming in!

00:12:53.270 --> 00:12:54.660
You're looking for Kazekoshi's room?

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:58.090
Sorry, but I don't know where 
the other schools' rooms are.

00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:00.250
It's at the end of the hall 
of the floor below us.

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:01.840
By the emergency exit.

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:03.820
Thanks a lot!

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:05.070
Let's go, Bundou!

00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:07.010
One moment please, Ikeda-senpai.

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:09.180
This!

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:13.110
You've got all the second 
edition star cards right here!

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:17.190
I collect pro mahjong player cards, too!

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:21.070
My second edition collection is still 
nowhere near complete, though!

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:22.380
This one!

00:13:22.380 --> 00:13:24.660
So this is this year's Kokaji?

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:26.010
I want this card so bad.

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:26.860
Bundou?

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:28.820
If I get an extra, you can have it.

00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:31.010
I have an extra Fujita.

00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:32.330
I don't want her.

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:34.410
What was that?

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:36.100
Pro player Fujita!

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:37.400
Uh, I just meant

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:39.130
that I already have your card,

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:40.520
I meant nothing else...

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:42.130
And what are you doing here?!

00:13:43.490 --> 00:13:45.380
You're Kajiki, right?

00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:47.650
Do you have some time?

00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:54.220
All they had were these huge yukatas...

00:13:54.660 --> 00:13:56.640
Then why don't you change 
back into your old clothes?

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:57.350
No way!

00:13:57.720 --> 00:14:00.980
Koromo is going to wear a yukata, 
like everyone else.

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:02.650
I want to match everyone else.

00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:04.660
That reminds me.

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:08.740
I think there was a small yukata 
in the stuff Hagiyoshi had packed.

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:10.110
Really?!

00:14:10.110 --> 00:14:12.490
He really is thorough.

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:14.290
Jun-kun! Koromo!

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:16.760
Kunihiro-kun, what's wrong?

00:14:16.760 --> 00:14:20.000
Touka... Something's weird about Touka!

00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:23.620
Huh? Isn't she always weird?

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:25.460
Yeah, but I don't mean that!

00:14:25.770 --> 00:14:29.740
It's just like when we were up against 
East Tokyo at last year's inter-high.

00:14:29.740 --> 00:14:31.010
She's like <i>that</i>!

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:32.040
Oh...

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:35.780
You mean she's in what you 
call the "Cold Touka" state.

00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:39.870
Touka met a large number of 
formidable opponents today.

00:14:40.370 --> 00:14:42.020
You're right.

00:14:42.550 --> 00:14:45.590
Whenever she gets around a 
large number of strong players,

00:14:45.590 --> 00:14:48.150
it changes her.

00:14:48.710 --> 00:14:53.240
The thing that the boy who married into 
Ryuumonbuchi feared became reality.

00:14:54.070 --> 00:14:57.790
If that means I get to play more 
unusual matches, Koromo is happy.

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:06.210
<i>But I'm not happy.</i>

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:15.880
And that's it!

00:15:15.880 --> 00:15:16.510
Ron!

00:15:16.510 --> 00:15:20.370
Richi and ippatsu only. 2,600!

00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:22.560
I guess there's such a 
thing as a cheap ippatsu.

00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:26.120
You can say stuff like 
that after you've beat me.

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:27.760
That's the spirit.

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:29.190
Please get stronger and stronger.

00:15:31.210 --> 00:15:31.860
Tsumo!

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:34.010
Mentanpin, sanshoku, two dora!

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:34.010
[Mentanpin: menzen (closed hand) + tanyao + pinfu]

00:15:34.010 --> 00:15:35.050
4,000 and 8,000.

00:15:35.050 --> 00:15:37.160
I won't even look at the ura dora!

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:39.720
Right, because with that 8 han pinfu,

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:42.120
getting ura dora wouldn't 
change the points you get.

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:43.650
The ura dora is a freebie!

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:44.150
<b>Annoyed</b>

00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:45.540
Just give me back 2,000 points.

00:15:47.530 --> 00:15:50.300
I made some rice balls and sandwiches.

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:52.530
I'll have one.

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:56.850
It's good!

00:15:57.860 --> 00:16:00.400
You've got a good captain.

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:03.290
A caring person who can 
play well and cook well.

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:04.840
You can't have her.

00:16:06.640 --> 00:16:09.650
Saki, come play with Koromo!

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:13.880
Wow, that table looks pretty intense.

00:16:13.880 --> 00:16:15.990
I sure don't want to join.

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:20.620
Then I think I'll join and play a serious 
game for the first time in a while.

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:29.550
Touka!

00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:33.470
Pleased to play with you.

00:16:43.990 --> 00:16:44.980
Kiyosumi?

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:46.360
Yeah.

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:48.880
Not Ryuumonbuchi?

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:51.860
It was Kiyosumi who beat Ryuumonbuchi.

00:16:52.840 --> 00:16:55.360
East Tokyo Representative
 Rinkai Girls' - 3rd Year
 Megan Davin

00:16:53.380 --> 00:16:55.360
That's too bad.

00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:57.790
You seem oddly hung up on them.

00:16:56.130 --> 00:16:58.550
East Tokyo Representative
 Rinkai Girls' - 3rd Year
 Tsujigaito Satoha

00:16:57.790 --> 00:16:59.080
Yes.

00:17:00.170 --> 00:17:02.080
I have regrets.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:06.080
Last year, that one player suddenly

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:08.510
transformed in the middle of the game.

00:17:09.690 --> 00:17:12.210
I redirected my attacks immediately

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:15.720
and knocked out Gappo Girls'.

00:17:16.900 --> 00:17:18.220
You mean you ran away.

00:17:19.090 --> 00:17:20.600
You're right.

00:17:21.940 --> 00:17:25.390
Last year, I faltered.

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:36.780
Tsumo!

00:17:37.630 --> 00:17:39.070
Ryuumonbuchi Touka!

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:41.200
<i>Damn!</i>

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:46.680
Ryuumonbuchi Touka   Amae Koromo    Fujita Yasuko    Miyanaga Saki

00:17:42.430 --> 00:17:45.420
I became afraid of her.

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:48.710
But this year...

00:17:49.810 --> 00:17:51.170
This year...

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:52.880
I'll defeat her face-to-face!

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:55.010
Yeah.

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:01.100
Touka!

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:02.180
You're awake.

00:18:03.240 --> 00:18:04.230
A dream?

00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:06.230
It was all just a dream?

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:08.850
If you're talking about your 
winning streak against Koromo,

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:10.130
Kiyosumi, and the pros...

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:11.310
It wasn't a dream.

00:18:14.560 --> 00:18:16.610
There was a person recording the tiles.

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:21.310
You fainted after the fourth match.

00:18:21.310 --> 00:18:22.870
I was really worried.

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:35.060
That Touka was really 
something though, huh?

00:18:35.060 --> 00:18:36.880
Even if she never had 
a flashy winning hand.

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:38.860
Even if it was still early,

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:40.960
her power over the 
tiles was stronger than

00:18:40.960 --> 00:18:42.510
Koromo's and the rinshan user's.

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:47.300
During that entire time, the river 
of discards was calm and quiet.

00:18:48.660 --> 00:18:52.020
<b>Okami                                         Water control</b>

00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:51.320
Water control...

00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:56.180
But I prefer the normal side of her 
that dives in with high momentum

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:59.390
right at the crucial moments.

00:19:01.380 --> 00:19:04.660
This... This is not me!

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:05.830
I reject it!

00:19:07.090 --> 00:19:07.950
Touka...

00:19:08.340 --> 00:19:12.000
This takes my style too far 
from Haramura Nodoka's!

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:13.000
<i>That's</i> your problem?

00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:18.840
That's...

00:19:19.920 --> 00:19:22.220
Speak of the devil. 
Takatoobara Middle School.

00:19:23.270 --> 00:19:26.040
That's the middle school 
Haramura Nodoka went to.

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:27.140
So that's why...

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:29.140
It's got nothing to do with that!

00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:30.880
<b>Kiyosumi High School 
Team Members</b>

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:33.950
Ryuumon-san was amazing.

00:19:33.950 --> 00:19:36.090
I couldn't get a single kan in.

00:19:36.090 --> 00:19:38.360
But that's normal.

00:19:39.720 --> 00:19:41.990
<i>Koromo-chan told me there 
were people at Nationals</i>

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:45.030
<i>who are good enough to 
knock out other players</i>

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:46.730
<i>even when she is in that state.</i>

00:19:51.770 --> 00:19:53.750
<i>I'm so excited!</i>

00:19:56.580 --> 00:19:57.630
Come in.

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:00.660
Hello!

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:01.340
Hello.

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:02.970
Who's that?

00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:05.010
I came!

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:06.580
Maho-chan!

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:08.390
It's the Muromaho Combo!

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:12.850
I went to the inter-middle 
school tournament with them.

00:20:14.150 --> 00:20:17.210
They said they wanted to come 
observe this training camp.

00:20:17.210 --> 00:20:19.470
I agreed to it.

00:20:19.470 --> 00:20:21.440
It's more fun when things are lively.

00:20:22.350 --> 00:20:25.310
Since they're already here, 
why don't we play a little?

00:20:25.310 --> 00:20:26.370
Saki, Nodoka?

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:27.950
Sounds good.

00:20:29.910 --> 00:20:30.860
Okay.

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:33.870
Thanks for letting us play!

00:20:43.860 --> 00:20:45.090
It's increased.

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:51.850
Good luck.

00:20:51.850 --> 00:20:53.590
The tacos are good.

00:20:53.590 --> 00:20:55.400
Thank you.

00:20:58.970 --> 00:21:01.940
<i>These tacos take me back.</i>

00:21:04.340 --> 00:21:07.410
<i>My idol, Nodoka-senpai, 
is right in front of me.</i>

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:12.160
<i>I guess it's been about four months 
since we've played together.</i>

00:21:12.590 --> 00:21:15.050
Is this tiny girl the one you talked about?

00:21:15.050 --> 00:21:16.090
That's right.

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:19.180
This is the first time 
I've seen her in person.

00:21:22.490 --> 00:21:23.930
You're here already?

00:21:23.930 --> 00:21:25.110
Yeah.

00:21:25.110 --> 00:21:26.320
What are those?

00:21:26.320 --> 00:21:29.430
Tile records from last year's 
inter-middle school tournament.

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:32.760
Oh, you mean for those two girls 
who joined the club yesterday?

00:21:32.760 --> 00:21:33.350
Yup.

00:21:33.860 --> 00:21:36.670
There's lots of records for Haramura-san,

00:21:36.670 --> 00:21:40.110
but for Kataoka-san there's only 
this one from the preliminary.

00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:46.650
But there's one more interesting 
person at this middle school.

00:21:47.220 --> 00:21:48.610
Ron!

00:21:48.610 --> 00:21:49.950
18,000.

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:51.700
Youch.

00:21:51.700 --> 00:21:53.910
An 18 hit right off the bat...

00:21:54.340 --> 00:21:56.750
That's the power of tacos!

00:21:57.350 --> 00:22:00.250
<i>An expensive win right from the start...</i>

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:02.300
<i>That's just like Yuuki-chan!</i>

00:22:02.300 --> 00:22:03.800
Tacos are amazing.

00:22:04.890 --> 00:22:08.920
<i>It's finally her debut...</i>

00:22:08.920 --> 00:22:12.350
<i>The star player of this camp has arrived!</i>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:49.940
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:49.940
<b>"Start"</b>

00:23:36.180 --> 00:23:39.270
Tokyo... What a terrifying city.

00:23:39.270 --> 00:23:41.130
Not only do they have loads 
of Mexican restaurants,

00:23:41.130 --> 00:23:43.620
but they also sell primo clothes here.

00:23:43.620 --> 00:23:46.120
Primo? Is that like a taco?

00:23:46.120 --> 00:23:48.030
Saki-san, she was talking about clothes...

00:23:49.940 --> 00:23:55.250
<b>Watch again!</b>
